Item 4 (breaker-gate.test.mjs EARS-M5 chmod test, panel finding LOW): this is a test-robustness
fix (a false-pass hazard under root), not a production-code bug, so there is no "RED against the
current behavior" to show in this repo — in this environment (OBSERVED: `id` -> uid=501, no
passwordless sudo) the test genuinely exercises the chmod write-failure path and passes for real,
with or without the guard.

Proved the guard is not vacuous by SIMULATING a root uid (no real root available here): a
throwaway harness overrides process.getuid() to return 0, then imports breaker-gate.test.mjs.
Result: the EARS-M5 test is reported SKIPPED with the stated reason; the other 13 tests still run
and pass (13 pass / 0 fail / 1 skipped) — the guard genuinely changes behavior under root instead
of being dead code.
